<!--
  kuna armconstshift all: a fixed 64-bit left shift of a signed operand is
  undefined C for negative values and for bits shifted into or past the sign,
  although every machine computes it modulo 2^64. P9 emission / cast-policy;
  P0 assertion `option armconstshift`. Two passes over LLVM objects for x86-64,
  AArch64, PowerPC64 and MIPS64 (tests/fixtures/wide-integer-emission/shift.c):
  `off` (the default) keeps upstream's `value << 0x1f`; `all` shifts the
  unsigned conversion, keeps a sign extension inside it and restores the signed
  result, while the shared store to *echo stays. The CLI companion
  wide_shift_emission.rs executes the `all` output under UBSan at O0/O2.
-->
